<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yohannes IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1837">1837</a>–<a href="/years/1889">1889</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Kassa Mercha, Yohannes IV of Ethiopia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yohannes IV was Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> from 1872 to 1889, a Tigrayan noble born <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosice">Kassa</a> Mercha who gained power with British arms after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tewodros-ii">Tewodros II</a>. He defeated Egyptian invasions at Gundet and Gura in 1875 and 1876 and resisted Italian expansion. He was killed fighting the Mahdist army at Gallabat (Metemma) in March 1889.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yohannes-iv.jpg" alt="Yohannes IV" width="320" height="502" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown but obviously dided 70 years ago · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yohannes_IV_-_4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
